  "scope": "Petersson integrability/definiteness and finite-coset pairing, using existing Mathlib hyperbolic volume; actual Gamma0 degeneracy maps and sparse Fourier formula; orthogonality arguments. The local oldspace includes all d*M | N from M<N, including d=1. No admitted general GLn or main-lemma proof is imported. Selected finite root-of-unity and convergent Fourier averaging proofs from QExpansionSlash; generalized from a prime to every positive integer. The full upstream Hecke/newform package is not imported. Selected rational-cusp transport from HeckeModularForm and finite Mobius/integral matrix calculations from HeckeT_p. The local prime invariance proof is specialized directly to Gamma0, including bad primes. Selected coprime divisor reindexing and prime-power arithmetic from FourierHecke are generalized locally to a completely multiplicative weight, allowing zero at bad primes. The actual determinant-normalized slash formula is proved locally; conflicting upstream normalization comments are not adopted. Selected abstract fundamental-domain transport from PeterssonLevelN and projective integer action/domain proofs from PSL2Action. Hyperbolic volume invariance reuses the pinned Mathlib instance; no duplicate Jacobian measure construction is ported. Selected adjugate matrix identities and integral Bezout representative from AdjointTheory. The local inverse-slash transport supplies the integral consumer; explicit Gamma0 upper/lower finite cosets are proved locally."
